Why don't we have something like : 

``` javascript
var instantsearch = require('instantsearch').make;
var search = instantsearch(appId, apiKey, indexName);
```

I'm not sure about the key used here (make) but I think that's easy to instanciate and use. Don't you think?

@algolia/javascript Are you ok with switching to:

``` js
var instantsearch = require('instantsearch');
var search = instantsearch(appId, apiKey, indexName);
```

Instead of:

``` js
var instantsearch = require('instantsearch');
var search = new instantsearch.InstantSearch(appId, apiKey, indexName);
```
